Carabiners of aluminum for climbing: CBP rulings classify them in 7616.99 (other articles of aluminum), but there is also 8308.90 (clasps... of base metal for clothing, footwear, awnings, handbags, travel goods). Climbing carabiners have been classified by CBP in 7616.99.5190 or 8302? Several rulings: "Carabiners... classified in subheading 7616.99.51, HTSUS, other articles of aluminum, other, other, other" — the older rulings used 7616.99.5090. Current: 7616.99.51 is "Other: Other: Other: Cast" or similar? The current HTSUS 7616.99: 7616.99.10 (Nails, tacks...?), 7616.99.20 (Cloth, grill, netting... ), 7616.99.30 (Fittings for tubes?), 7616.99.50 "Other: Articles of aluminum, other: Other: Cast" hmm. Actually 7616.99.51 is "Other: Other: Cast-aluminum articles"? I recall 7616.99.5130 "Other, Other: Of cast" ... Actually 7616.99.51 "Other" 7616.99.5190 "Other" under 7616.99.51 "Other: Other: Other". I'll go with 7616.99.5190.

However, a ruling for locking carabiners in sports (mountaineering) could be 8308.90.30? Aluminum predominant with plastic components; I'll stay with 7616.99.5190.

{"hts_code": "7616.99.5190", "reason": "Locking climbing carabiners with aluminum as the predominant material are non-electric other articles of aluminum, classified in 7616.99 as other articles of aluminum."}
